---
import { BASH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS } from '../../consts/product';
import { SNIPPETS } from '../../consts/snippets';
import { minutesLong } from '../../lib/format';
import CodeCard from '../CodeCard.astro';
import ChatDemo from '../demos/ChatDemo.astro';
import RuleList from '../RuleList.astro';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
---

<Section id="on-demand" heading="Long commands in the background, a free chat for your user">
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    Some tools are fast most of the time and slow some of the time. <code class="ic">bash</code> is the classic case:
    <code class="ic">ls</code> takes a millisecond, the full test suite takes twenty minutes.
  </Fragment>
  <p class="t-body">With an <strong>on-demand</strong> background tool, the model picks the mode call by call:</p>
  <RuleList>
    <li>
      <strong>A normal call</strong> runs right away inside the turn, and the model reads the output immediately, like any tool.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A call with <code class="ic">run_in_background: true</code></strong> becomes a background task. The agent replies,
      and the user can keep chatting about something else while the command runs.
    </li>
  </RuleList>
  <p class="t-body">
    Here a normal <code class="ic">bash</code> call keeps its usual short time limit, while a background call may run for
    {minutesLong(BASH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS.background / 60)}. You don't have to explain any of this in your prompts: the toolkit
    tells the model which tools run in the background, when to use <code class="ic">run_in_background</code>, and how to read
    results when they arrive.
  </p>
  <p class="t-body">
    For tools that are <em>always</em> slow, such as a deployment, skip <code class="ic">onDemand()</code>: every call then runs
    in the background, and the model sees the tool as <code class="ic">deploy_background</code>.
  </p>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <ChatDemo name="bash" agent="Dev agent" thread="DevAgent · thread 3b90af" height="xl" />
    <CodeCard title="PHP" snippet={SNIPPETS.onDemand} />
  </Fragment>
</Section>
